{"toolCallId":"call_56b3663d780b4584bfe79cac29e122f0","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\nN/A — record any testing beyond the verification tasks in `tasks.md` here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\nN/A — record dependencies beyond the components named in the architecture here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\nN/A — record rollback steps beyond reverting the scoped change here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Change one Bash script: parse and validate a --min-percent threshold, evaluate it after the report is written, and return exit code 3 below it while leaving the report byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\n  - \"min-percent threshold gate\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - standalone CLI under `runtime/cli/spec/` |\n| **Storage** | None - reads spec folder files and writes a temporary stats directory |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, `shellcheck` when installed, and command-level exit-code and `diff` checks |\n\n### Overview\nChange one script in three places: the argument loop gains `--min-percent` with range validation, the threshold is evaluated after the report writer returns, and the help plus exit-code comment block document it. The report writers stay untouched, so the proof is a `diff` of the report with and without the flag plus an exit-code matrix around the boundary.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nOther - single-file Bash CLI with a straight-line flow.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`case \"$1\"` loop, section 8): gains the `--min-percent` branch, its missing-value guard and the 0-100 range check.\n- **Report writers** (`output_text`, `output_json`): unchanged; the gate runs after they finish, which is what keeps the report byte-identical.\n- **Threshold gate** (new, between the report writer call and the final `exit 0`): compares the active mode's percentage with `MIN_PERCENT` and returns 3 or 0.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser (sets `MIN_PERCENT`, `SPEC_FOLDER`, `SINGLE_FILE`) → `calculate_file_completeness` or `calculate_spec_completeness` → report writer → threshold gate → exit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nVerification uses two inputs. The packet folder itself reports 100 percent once its docs are filled, which proves the top of the range. A fixture in `scratch/fixture/spec.md` with two `[TBD]` tokens across four content lines reports exactly 50 percent, which gives a deterministic mid-range boundary without depending on any real packet's state.\n\nCommands, in order:\n- `bash -n` on the script, and `shellcheck` when it is installed.\n- Boundary matrix on the fixture: `--min-percent 51` exits 3, `50` exits 0, `49` exits 0.\n- Top of range on the packet: `--min-percent 100` exits 0.\n- Parity: `diff` of the text report and of the `--json` report, each with and without `--min-percent 0`.\n- Invalid input: missing value, `abc`, `-1`, `101` each exit 1 with `ERROR:` on stderr and no report.\n- `--file` mode: the threshold follows the printed `Completion` value.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\nBash 3.2 or later, `bc`, `grep`, `find` and `sed` - all already required by the script. No new package and no new runtime.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the report changes without the flag, or a caller that omits the option sees a new exit code. Action: revert the single script file. There is no state, schema or data migration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":23,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":21}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
