like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. GOOD: Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only the recommended-level line. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With `--quiet`, stdout holds exactly one line that starts with `Recommended Level:`. WEAK: The flag should work well. -->\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A caller parses the level line and breaks when the label changes. Mitigation: keep the label stable and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does `--quiet` also suppress warnings on stderr? Decision: no, stderr is unchanged. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh always exits 0 when its calculation succeeds, so a caller that wants to fail below a completion threshold has to parse the report. Add a --min-percent <N> option that turns that comparison into an exit code while leaving the report unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\n  - \"min-percent exit code\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `detached HEAD (scaffolded with --skip-branch)` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` computes an Overall Completion percentage and always exits 0 when the calculation succeeds, so a CI job or gate script that wants \"fail below N percent\" has to capture stdout and parse the report. That parsing duplicates the script's arithmetic, differs between the text and JSON forms, and breaks silently when the report wording changes.\n\n### Purpose\nLet any caller gate on a completion threshold with a single exit-code check, while the existing report stays byte-identical.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `--min-percent <N>` option parsing with integer range validation for `N` between 0 and 100.\n- Return exit code 3 after the report when completion is below `N`, and exit code 0 otherwise.\n- Apply the same threshold in `--file` mode against that mode's reported `Completion` value.\n- Document the option in `show_help` and in the script's trailing exit-code comment block.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing how completion is calculated - the placeholder-to-line ratio is the contract this flag reads, not something it redefines.\n- Changing the text or JSON report - callers that parse the report today must see identical bytes.\n- Wiring the flag into `validate.sh` or `check-completion.sh` - those are separate callers and a separate change.\n- Adding a short alias such as `-m` - no caller needs one, and the short flags in this script are already assigned.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Parse and validate `--min-percent`, gate the exit code on the reported percentage, and document the option |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` with an integer `N` between 0 and 100. | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent` completes with exit 0 or 3, never 1. |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below `N`. | On a folder reporting `Overall Completion: 42%`, `--min-percent 43` exits 3 while `--min-percent 42` exits 0. |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above `N`, including `N=0`. | `--min-percent 0` exits 0 on every folder that calculates successfully. |\n| REQ-004 | Keep the report byte-identical with and without the option. | `diff` between the plain report and the `--min-percent 0` report is empty, in both text and `--json` mode. |\n| REQ-005 | Reject an invalid value before calculating anything. | A missing value, `abc`, `-1` and `101` each print an `ERROR:` line on stderr, print no report, and exit 1. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-006 | Document the option where the script already documents its interface. | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` and the trailing exit-code comment block names 3 as the below-threshold code. |\n| REQ-007 | Apply the threshold in `--file` mode against that file's `Completion` value. | `--file <path> --min-percent 100` exits 3 for a file below 100 percent and 0 for a file at 100 percent. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: A caller gates with one check: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 80 <folder>; echo $?` prints 3 below 80 and 0 at or above it.\n- **SC-002**: `diff` of the text report and of the `--json` report, each with and without `--min-percent 0`, prints nothing.\n- **SC-003**: `--help` names the option, and `bash -n` on the script exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc` for the percentage arithmetic | The script already exits 1 when `bc` is missing, so the flag adds no dependency | Leave the existing `command -v bc` preflight untouched |\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2, the macOS `/bin/bash` the script targets | A construct such as `local -n` or an associative array would break the target shell | Use only `[[ ]]` integer comparison and plain scalars, as the rest of the script does |\n| Risk | Exit code 3 collides with the spec CLI taxonomy, where 3 means system error | Medium | Document 3 as below-threshold in the script's exit-code block and `--help`, so callers of this script read it unambiguously |\n| Risk | `$2` is unbound under `set -u` when `--min-percent` is the last argument | Low | Read `${2:-}`, emit the standard `ERROR:` line and exit 1 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. Resolved during planning: `--file` mode prints `Completion:` rather than `Overall Completion:`, so the threshold reads that mode's percentage; folder mode reads `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":30,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":28}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d2f4c4967e374f7b9f6f985e7b160194","title":"Read lines 1-45 in /private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/devin-overflows-501/ef6cddb7/content.txt","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"sed -n '1,45p' /var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/devin-overflows-501/ef6cddb7/content.txt","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"sed -n '1,45p' /var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/devin-overflows-501/ef6cddb7/content.txt"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["sed"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_de8c38bff67e466c8fcfe8355cd4067d","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Change one Bash script: parse and validate a --min-percent threshold, evaluate it after the report is written, and return exit code 3 below it while leaving the report byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\n  - \"min-percent threshold gate\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - standalone CLI under `runtime/cli/spec/` |\n| **Storage** | None - reads spec folder files and writes a temporary stats directory |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, `shellcheck` when installed, and command-level exit-code and `diff` checks |\n\n### Overview\nChange one script in three places: the argument loop gains `--min-percent` with range validation, the threshold is evaluated after the report writer returns, and the help plus exit-code comment block document it. The report writers stay untouched, so the proof is a `diff` of the report with and without the flag plus an exit-code matrix around the boundary.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nOther - single-file Bash CLI with a straight-line flow.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`case \"$1\"` loop, section 8): gains the `--min-percent` branch, its missing-value guard and the 0-100 range check.\n- **Report writers** (`output_text`, `output_json`): unchanged; the gate runs after they finish, which is what keeps the report byte-identical.\n- **Threshold gate** (new, between the report writer call and the final `exit 0`): compares the active mode's percentage with `MIN_PERCENT` and returns 3 or 0.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser (sets `MIN_PERCENT`, `SPEC_FOLDER`, `SINGLE_FILE`) → `calculate_file_completeness` or `calculate_spec_completeness` → report writer → threshold gate → exit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nVerification uses two inputs. The packet folder itself reports 100 percent once its docs are filled, which proves the top of the range. A fixture in `scratch/fixture/spec.md` with two `[TBD]` tokens across four content lines reports exactly 50 percent, which gives a deterministic mid-range boundary without depending on any real packet's state.\n\nCommands, in order:\n- `bash -n` on the script, and `shellcheck` when it is installed.\n- Boundary matrix on the fixture: `--min-percent 51` exits 3, `50` exits 0, `49` exits 0.\n- Top of range on the packet: `--min-percent 100` exits 0.\n- Parity: `diff` of the text report and of the `--json` report, each with and without `--min-percent 0`.\n- Invalid input: missing value, `abc`, `-1`, `101` each exit 1 with `ERROR:` on stderr and no report.\n- `--file` mode: the threshold follows the printed `Completion` value.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\nBash 3.2 or later, `bc`, `grep`, `find` and `sed` - all already required by the script. No new package and no new runtime.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the report changes without the flag, or a caller that omits the option sees a new exit code. Action: revert the single script file. There is no state, schema or data migration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Change one Bash script: parse and validate a --min-percent threshold, evaluate it after the report is written, and return exit code 3 below it while leaving the report byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\n  - \"min-percent threshold gate\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - standalone CLI under `runtime/cli/spec/` |\n| **Storage** | None - reads spec folder files and writes a temporary stats directory |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, `shellcheck` when installed, and command-level exit-code and `diff` checks |\n\n### Overview\nChange one script in three places: the argument loop gains `--min-percent` with range validation, the threshold is evaluated after the report writer returns, and the help plus exit-code comment block document it. The report writers stay untouched, so the proof is a `diff` of the report with and without the flag plus an exit-code matrix around the boundary.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nOther - single-file Bash CLI with a straight-line flow.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`case \"$1\"` loop, section 8): gains the `--min-percent` branch, its missing-value guard and the 0-100 range check.\n- **Report writers** (`output_text`, `output_json`): unchanged; the gate runs after they finish, which is what keeps the report byte-identical.\n- **Threshold gate** (new, between the report writer call and the final `exit 0`): compares the active mode's percentage with `MIN_PERCENT` and returns 3 or 0.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser (sets `MIN_PERCENT`, `SPEC_FOLDER`, `SINGLE_FILE`) → `calculate_file_completeness` or `calculate_spec_completeness` → report writer → threshold gate → exit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nVerification uses two inputs. The packet folder itself reports 100 percent once its docs are filled, which proves the top of the range. A fixture in `scratch/fixture/spec.md` with two placeholder tokens across four content lines reports exactly 50 percent, which gives a deterministic mid-range boundary without depending on any real packet's state.\n\nCommands, in order:\n- `bash -n` on the script, and `shellcheck` when it is installed.\n- Boundary matrix on the fixture: `--min-percent 51` exits 3, `50` exits 0, `49` exits 0.\n- Top of range on the packet: `--min-percent 100` exits 0.\n- Parity: `diff` of the text report and of the `--json` report, each with and without `--min-percent 0`.\n- Invalid input: missing value, `abc`, `-1`, `101` each exit 1 with `ERROR:` on stderr and no report.\n- `--file` mode: the threshold follows the printed `Completion` value.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\nBash 3.2 or later, `bc`, `grep`, `find` and `sed` - all already required by the script. No new package and no new runtime.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the report changes without the flag, or a caller that omits the option sees a new exit code. Action: revert the single script file. There is no state, schema or data migration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
