{"toolCallId":"call_ff2851685c114ab7babfe8957769d4c5","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Fourteen ordered tasks across setup, implementation and verification for the --min-percent option, each with a command that proves it.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\n  - \"min-percent implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n`S` is the script under change: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `P` is this packet: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Create the mid-range fixture (`$P/scratch/fixture/spec.md`). Write `# Fixture`, two `[TBD]` lines and one `Content line`. Verify: `bash $S $P/scratch/fixture | rg 'Overall Completion'` prints `Overall Completion: 50%`.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the text baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-text.txt`). Run `bash $S $P > $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt` before any edit. Verify: `rg -c 'Overall Completion: 100%' $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the JSON baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt`). Run `bash $S --json $P > $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` before any edit. Verify: `rg -c '\"overall_completion\": 100' $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the threshold global (`$S`). Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside `SINGLE_FILE` in the globals block. Verify: `rg -n '^MIN_PERCENT=' $S` prints exactly one line.\n- [ ] T005 Parse and validate the option (`$S`). Add a `--min-percent)` branch that reads `${2:-}`, rejects an empty value, a non-integer and a value outside 0-100 with an `ERROR: --min-percent` line on stderr and exit 1, and otherwise assigns `MIN_PERCENT` and shifts two. Verify: `bash $S --min-percent abc $P; echo $?` prints the `ERROR:` line then `1`.\n- [ ] T006 Gate the exit code (`$S`). After the report writer call and before the final `exit 0`, compare `MIN_PERCENT` with `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and with the single-file stats `percentage` in `--file` mode, exiting 3 when the value is lower. Verify: `bash $S --min-percent 51 $P/scratch/fixture; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T007 Document the option (`$S`). Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and a `3 - Below --min-percent threshold` line to the trailing exit-code comment block. Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -- '--min-percent'` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Text report parity (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt <(bash $S --min-percent 0 $P)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T009 JSON report parity (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt <(bash $S --json --min-percent 0 $P)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Threshold boundary matrix (`$S`). Verify: `--min-percent 51` on the fixture exits 3, `50` exits 0 and `49` exits 0.\n- [ ] T011 Top of range (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent 100 $P; echo $?` prints `0` because the packet reports 100 percent.\n- [ ] T012 Invalid input matrix (`$S`). Verify: `--min-percent` with no value, `abc`, `-1` and `101` each exit 1, print `ERROR:` on stderr and print no `Overall Completion` line.\n- [ ] T013 Single-file mode (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --file $P/scratch/fixture/spec.md --min-percent 51; echo $?` prints `3`, and the same call with `50` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T014 Syntax and lint (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0, and `shellcheck $S` reports nothing when shellcheck is installed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of the text report and of the JSON report, with and without `--min-percent`, is empty\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":19,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":20}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
